# Test / capture video, and never in the repo.
# `[2026-09-15]` The video-capture tests (shell/linux/integration-tests case 5,
# and the driven Captures / branch-export panels) MUST produce a real file -
# "the AVI has pictures in it" cannot be checked without one - so the file is
# necessary during the test. It is written to a mktemp dir or an XDG_DATA_HOME
# under /tmp and deleted once the check has read it; a real user's exports live
# under ~/.local/share/flycast-dojo/captures, not here. These patterns are the
# belt-and-suspenders: if the emulator is ever run with the repo as its working
# directory, a CWD-relative `captures/` (the fork's avi_dump path) would land in
# the tree, and a 2.4 GB MJPEG must never be committable by accident.
*.avi
*.mov
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.pcm
captures/
